figdown "0.1" block
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: RULE 2.4's enum half at the two header positions
# (vocabulary-sources.tsv `figdown.version`, `figdown.genre`). The quoting is
# reported BEFORE the value and suppresses it for that token — one token, one
# error, the convention every id position has followed. Both
# values below are well spelled, so only the quoting is wrong; a QUOTED and
# misspelled genre reports the quoting alone too.
node a "A"
figdown 0.1 "block"
node b "B"
figdown 0.1 "blok"
node c "C"
